From: Caner Altinbasak <cal@brightsign.biz>
Date: Thu, 12 Feb 2026 15:33:09 +0000
Subject: feat: Enable cross-process memory pressure notification on all
 platforms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chromium's browser-to-renderer memory pressure IPC (via
mojom::ChildProcess::OnMemoryPressure) is gated behind IS_ANDROID. This
patch removes the platform guard so that the browser process can
programmatically trigger memory pressure notifications in renderer
processes on all platforms.

This enables Electron's memoryPressureMonitor.notifyMemoryPressure() API
to propagate pressure signals to all renderer processes, causing blink,
V8, and other subsystems to release cached memory.

The infrastructure is identical to what ships on Android — we are simply
enabling it on Linux, macOS, and Windows.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
index de5b4e88f20d8f98253799bdf0c85c08feb07c2e..60e913f989beedb65d9a269e17159d07eb69702c 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
@@ -6261,6 +6261,11 @@ void RenderProcessHostImpl::ProvideSwapFileForRenderer() {
           std::move(allocator)));
 }
 
+void RenderProcessHostImpl::NotifyMemoryPressureToRenderer(
+    base::MemoryPressureLevel level) {
+  child_process_->OnMemoryPressure(level);
+}
+
 void RenderProcessHostImpl::GetBoundInterfacesForTesting(
     std::vector<std::string>& out) {
   io_thread_host_impl_->AsyncCall(&IOThreadHostImpl::GetInterfacesForTesting)
diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.h b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.h
index 3f5d4fc3777ae71b4bf652f02afca72f9b2e5c39..1701577b0cc94ac40fc570ce1d138e4ee225b150 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.h
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.h
@@ -894,6 +894,10 @@ class CONTENT_EXPORT RenderProcessHostImpl
       GlobalRenderFrameHostId render_frame_host_id);
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_P2P_ENABLED)
 
+   // Notifies the renderer process of memory pressure level.
+   void NotifyMemoryPressureToRenderer(
+       base::MemoryPressureLevel level);
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(ALLOW_OOP_VIDEO_DECODER)
   using VideoDecoderFactoryCreationCB = base::RepeatingCallback<void(
       mojo::PendingReceiver<media::mojom::InterfaceFactory>)>;
